<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n107775" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑπέροχ-ος</span></b> , 
			Ep.
		 and 
			Ion.
		
		<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑπείρ-</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>, (<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑπερέχω</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					11
				</span></i>
			) <i>prominent, eminent, distinguished above</i> others, c.
			gen., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑπείροχον ἔμμεναι ἄλλων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					6.208
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				11.784
			</span></i>: abs., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑπείροχον εἶδος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>h.Hom.</u>
					12.2
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οἱ ὑπέροχοι</span> (
				v.l.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑπείροχοι</span>
			)
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc"> τῶν ἀστῶν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hdt.
					5.92
				</span></i>
			. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ή</span>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θῆρες ἐν πελάγεϊ ὑπέροχοι</span>”
				<i>mighty,</i>
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pi.
					<u>N.</u>
					3.24
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑπέροχον σθένος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.
					<u>Pr.</u>
					428
				</span></i>
			 (lyr.); <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑπέροχος βία</span>
			<i>overbearing</i> force, <i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>Tr.</u>
				1096
			</span></i> codd. (sed leg. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">βίᾳ</span>); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑ. Νίκα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					B.
					3.5
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">συρικτὰν μέγ᾽ ὑπείροχον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Theoc.
					7.28
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οἰωνῶν μέγ᾽ ὑ. ἀγγελιώτην</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Call.
					<u>Jov.</u>
					68
				</span></i>
			: 
				Sup.
			
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑπεροχώτατος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pi.
					<u>P.</u>
					2.38
				</span></i>
			 (as a title, <i><span class="en">
				<u>PMasp.</u>
				4.5
			</span></i>
			<span class="entity">(vi A.D.)</span>): neut. pl. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑπείροχα</span> as Adv., <i><span class="en">
				<u>IG</u>
				12(5).678.21
			</span></i> (Syros, metr.).</div>
